!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-definition-mark-with-no-definition-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §12.1"
  description: """
    At the head of a type definition the two words are marks unconditionally, so `pet => abstract` is a
    declaration missing its definition rather than an alias of the record declared above it. This is the
    whole of the reservation the marks make, and it is what keeps `mid => abstract base & { … }`
    writable: a marked composition and an alias differ only in what follows the head, so reading the
    word conditionally would have to give one of them up.

    The companion valid vector shows the other side -- both words remain ordinary names at every
    position but this one.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
